      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It would be nice to change the camera color based on whether or not Streamer Mode is activated in settings. Some streamers are afraid of announcing that they are streaming due to fear of being harassed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-09T08:33:24.379Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For two reasons:\n1) It should be common courtesy to know that someone might be streaming or recording.\n2) I use the Photo Camera a lot to keep track of the facial expressions on my avatar, and keep an eye on the tracking, and I'm tired of being mistaken for a streamer while in public, when I'm not. I hang out in spaces where having your camera out is almost the norm, so someone having a camera out in itself is not a good indicator that they might be streaming or recording.\nI know at least one other Social VR game where the Stream Camera equivalent does make a \"LIVE\" tag show up next to your nameplate. Although it wouldn't have to be as obvious. Just making the lens a different color or shape, for instance would be enough.\nI guess number 2 could be solved with a local-only hand-held mirror that you could always use or similar, though.",
